course: dictionary
lesson: 10746
title: Uranium: a heavy metal with a big job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uranium is a noun, the name of a metal. Its context gives you clues. «In a nuclear power station, uranium atoms split and give off heat, which makes steam to spin turbines.» Power station, heat and steam tell you that uranium is a source of energy.
explain: The word radioactive is new, but the sentence explains it. Uranium atoms split and give off energy and radiation, so radioactive means a substance that sends out energy and rays on its own. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check.
explain: «A small pellet of uranium fuel holds about as much energy as a tonne of coal.» A pellet is tiny and a tonne is very heavy, so the comparison tells you uranium packs a huge amount of energy into a small space. Clues in the words around a new word can teach you a lot.
fact: Uranium is a heavy, silvery, radioactive metal found in rocks.
fact: Uranium has the symbol U and the atomic number 92.
fact: Uranium is used as fuel in nuclear power stations and in nuclear weapons.
fact: Nuclear power stations use uranium to make heat, which boils water into steam to drive turbines.
fact: Uranium is named after the planet Uranus.
exercise: «In a nuclear power station, uranium atoms split and give off heat.» What does uranium do in this sentence? | It is a plastic used to make pipes | It is a gas that floats up into the air | *It is a fuel whose atoms split and give off heat | It cools the water down
exercise: What is uranium? | A type of sugar | Water kept very cold | *A heavy, silvery, radioactive metal found in rocks | A wooden tool used by miners
exercise: Which symbol stands for uranium on the periodic table? | Ur | Ra | *U | Un
test: Uranium is named after which planet? | Mars | Venus | *Uranus | Neptune
test: «A small pellet of uranium fuel holds about as much energy as a tonne of coal.» What does this tell you? | Pellets are always bigger than tonnes | Coal is lighter than air | *Uranium fuel packs a huge amount of energy into a small amount | Uranium is soft and easy to cut
exam: Which sentence about uranium is true? | *Uranium is a radioactive metal used as fuel in nuclear power stations | Uranium is a liquid that is used to make bread | Uranium is a gas that is found in the sea | Uranium is a plant that grows in forests
